WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.550
Now the migration trap.

2
00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:05.800
Ownership records only help if the
old and new systems agree on them.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.875
Infoblox's default mode, Interim,
checks ownership with TXT records.

4
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:15.963
Its Standard mode uses DHCID records,
the format the standards define.

5
00:00:15.963 --> 00:00:20.000
Infoblox documents three cases
where TXT checking fails.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.454
First, migration from Microsoft-based
systems: those records have no TXT,

7
00:00:25.454 --> 00:00:30.363
and, in Infoblox's words, new DDNS
updates fail after the migration.

8
00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:34.738
Second, a mix of Microsoft
and ISC DHCP servers.

9
00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:37.572
Third, mobility: a
laptop's wired and Wi-Fi

10
00:00:37.572 --> 00:00:40.750
interfaces look like
two different clients.

11
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.875
The second trap is on Macs.

12
00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:46.035
Apple's private Wi-Fi
address feature gives a Mac a

13
00:00:46.035 --> 00:00:49.888
different hardware address, its
MAC address, on each network.

14
00:00:49.888 --> 00:00:53.484
Fixed is the default on
WPA2 or better networks;

15
00:00:53.484 --> 00:00:56.988
Rotating changes the
address every two weeks.

16
00:00:56.988 --> 00:01:01.438
An MDM, mobile device management,
profile can turn it off with a key

17
00:01:01.438 --> 00:01:06.549
called DisableAssociationMACRandomization,
on macOS fifteen and later.

18
00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:10.839
As an inference, a rotating
address changes the DHCP identity

19
00:01:10.839 --> 00:01:14.875
that ownership records rest
on, the same mobility failure.

20
00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:18.125
I didn't verify the Android
or Windows equivalents.

21
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:22.145
The program design guidance:
pick Standard or Interim once,

22
00:01:22.145 --> 00:01:27.150
migrate deliberately, and turn off
address randomization on agency Wi-Fi.

23
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.637
Sources: Infoblox NIOS 9.1:

24
00:01:29.637 --> 00:01:36.388
Enabling DDNS for IPv4 and IPv6 DHCP
Clients (Interim vs Standard) [S45],

25
00:01:36.388 --> 00:01:42.074
Configuring DDNS Update
Verification [S46]; Apple Support,

26
00:01:42.074 --> 00:01:46.811
Use private Wi-Fi addresses
on Apple devices [S49];

27
00:01:46.811 --> 00:01:52.378
apple/device-management
com.apple.wifi.managed.yaml [S50];

28
00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:58.130
research checklist steps 6 and
7 (program design guidance).
